---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Snake Game Online"
  description="Snake Game's privacy policy. We collect no personal data, store your scores only in your browser, and use anonymous analytics. Learn exactly what we do and don't track."
  eyebrow="PRIVACY POLICY"
  heading="Your privacy, kept simple."
  kicker="This page explains what Snake Game collects, what it stores, and what it never touches. The short version: we don't ask for personal data, and the game works fully on your device."
>
  <h2>Last updated</h2>
  <p>August 20, 2026</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    Snake Game is a client-side game. It runs entirely in your browser, and we operate no user
    accounts and no login system. We do <strong>not</strong> collect your name, email address,
    or any other personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>Local storage on your device</h2>
  <p>
    To make the game feel instant and work offline, Snake Game saves some data in your
    browser's <strong>local storage</strong>. This stays on your device and never leaves it.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Best scores and best lengths</strong> for each game mode.</li>
    <li><strong>Your Daily challenge history and streak.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Preferences</strong> such as your sound setting and chosen mode.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Clearing your browser's site data will reset these. Because it all lives in your browser,
    it is never shared with us or with anyone else.
  </p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use Google Analytics (GA4) to understand aggregate usage — for example, how many people
    play each mode and how often runs end. These events are anonymous and do not include
    personal data, and they help us keep the game fast and fix what breaks. Google Analytics is
    provided by Google LLC and may set its own cookies; its handling of that data is governed by
    Google's privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Snake Game itself does not set cookies. Google Analytics, described above, may set cookies
    in line with its own policies. You can block or delete cookies in your browser at any time
    without losing the ability to play.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> (Google LLC) — anonymous usage analytics.</li>
    <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (GitHub, Inc.) — hosting for the game.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Neither service is used to track you across the site for advertising, and we show no ads.</p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Snake Game is appropriate for all ages and collects no personal information from anyone,
    including children under 13. If you believe a child has submitted personal data to us,
    <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}contact/`}>contact us</a> and we will remove it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change anything about how the game handles your data, we will update this page. The
    "Last updated" date at the top reflects the most recent change.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy? Email us at
    <a href="mailto:yashkharb37@gmail.com">yashkharb37@gmail.com</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>